@page "/sources"
@using BibleAtlas.Client.State
@using BibleAtlas.Client.Views
@inject AtlasClient Atlas
@inject StateAtom<ViewArrangement> ViewArrangementAtom

@* Batch S ("document our sources for everything and give it a dedicated
   page on the site"): the app's ONE decisive home for attribution --
   MainLayout's own "Credits" header link now points straight here (see
   MainLayout.razor's `attribution` anchor), replacing the popover it used
   to open. This page renders ENTIRELY from `AtlasClient.Sources()` (`GET
   /api/sources`, itself generated 1:1 from LICENSES.md -- see
   `server/atlas-etl/src/sources.rs`'s own doc comment): no hardcoded
   duplicate credit list lives anywhere in this client (requirement 3).

   Styling: design-direction.md's "quiet parchment" direction -- this is
   reading material, not a legal dump, so it gets its own page-root class
   (never combined with .reader-page/.world-page -- "each page's root
   element carries one of these two classes" governs THOSE two; a third
   distinct page root is the correct, single-class-selector way to add a
   third material, not stacking a second class onto an existing one).

   Batch VC-1 (R4, the generality proof): Sources declares its own
   enter-split hatch ("read-beside," Kind "enter-split," partner
   ViewNames.Reader) and, when it wins ownership of the split-h HOST slot,
   embeds a CompositionSplit of its own -- the SAME mechanism Reader.razor
   already uses, not a bespoke copy. This is genuinely the generality proof
   the owner ordered: Sources was never privileged as a host before this
   batch (it had no split awareness at all); now it hosts exactly the same
   way Reader always could, proving "no privileged split host" for real,
   not just in the type system. No follow chip/link renders here at all --
   Sources declares no BearsWindow (or BearsLocus) capability, so
   World.razor's own _follow predicate (the ONE place that capability query
   runs) is unreachable for this pairing by construction; see that
   property's own comment.

   Fix round 1 (Adjudication F): the SplitDivider/width-state/role-
   determination glue this page used to duplicate from Reader.razor is
   GONE -- CompositionSplit owns all of it now, shared, not copied. This
   page's own remaining job is exactly what it always should have been:
   render its OWN content, and tell CompositionSplit which role-specific
   button to show via `ctx`.

   Fix round 2 (ruling 1/3, N-1 -- re-review): the ViewArrangementAtom
   subscription this page used to carry (`Changed += / -= OnViewArrangementChanged`,
   `@implements IDisposable`) is GONE too -- CompositionSplit now owns that
   subscription exactly once (see its own header, RULING 1) and this page's
   ENTIRE markup lives inside `<CompositionSplit>`'s own ChildContent, so
   its re-render already covers everything Sources needs; there was never a
   genuine per-host need here (unlike Reader.razor -- see that page's own
   comment for the one documented exception). This IS the "declare a hatch,
   nothing else" minimal host CompositionSplit.razor's own header now
   documents as the official recipe -- read this page as that reference
   example. *@

<PageTitle>Bible Explorer &mdash; Sources</PageTitle>

<CompositionSplit HostName="@ViewNames.Sources" SplitModeOverride="@SplitMode" HostPaneClass="split-pane-host" Context="ctx">
    <div class="@($"sources-page{ctx.HostPaneClassSuffix}")" data-testid="sources-page">
        <div class="sources-column">
            <h1 class="sources-title">Sources</h1>
            <p class="sources-intro">
                Bible Explorer stands on the work of translators, researchers, and
                scholars across many centuries. Every source below is honestly
                named: what it is, what we built from it, and its license.
            </p>

            @if (!ctx.IsSplitOpen)
            {
                <button type="button" class="split-open split-open-parchment" data-testid="split-open-sources"
                        @onclick="ctx.InvokeHatch">
                    Read beside the reader
                </button>
            }

            @if (_error is not null)
            {
                <div class="toast" data-testid="toast">
                    <p class="toast-message">@_error</p>
                </div>
            }
            else if (_doc is null)
            {
                <p class="sources-loading">Loading sources&hellip;</p>
            }
            else
            {
                @foreach (var category in _doc.Categories)
                {
                    <section class="sources-category" data-testid="sources-category-@category.Id">
                        <h2 class="sources-category-title">@category.Label</h2>
                        <div class="sources-grid">
                            @foreach (var source in SourcesFor(category.Id))
                            {
                                <article class="source-card" data-testid="source-@source.Id">
                                    <h3 class="source-title">@source.Title</h3>
                                    <p class="source-what">@source.WhatItIs</p>
                                    <p class="source-built"><span class="source-label">What we built:</span> @source.WhatWeBuilt</p>
                                    <p class="source-license"><span class="source-label">License:</span> @source.License</p>
                                    @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(source.Link))
                                    {
                                        <a class="source-link" data-testid="source-link-@source.Id" href="@source.Link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit source</a>
                                    }
                                </article>
                            }
                        </div>
                    </section>
                }
            }
        </div>
    </div>
</CompositionSplit>

@code {
    private SourcesDocumentOut? _doc;
    private string? _error;

    // Batch VC-1: null = self-determine (Sources is always routed directly
    // -- there is no scenario in this batch where Sources is mounted as
    // someone ELSE's guest). Fix round 1: no longer paired with an IsHost/
    // OnRequestClose parameter -- CompositionSplit computes both internally
    // from SplitMode alone now (see that component's own header).
    //
    // Fix round 2 (Q-4, trivia -- re-review, PARTIAL, "Sources.SplitMode
    // remains dead ... with no test keeping it coherent. Symmetry argument
    // unchanged and still defensible"): true today -- ViewRegistrySetup's
    // own Sources mount closure (the ONE thing that would ever set this
    // non-null) is registered but never invoked, since no shipped pairing
    // hosts Sources as ITS guest yet. Kept anyway, deliberately: Reader and
    // World BOTH carry this identical parameter/null-check shape (a routed
    // view is either self-determined or registry-mounted, the SAME two
    // cases for every registered view by construction, per R1), and Sources
    // is registered in that SAME registry (ViewRegistrySetup.Build) with
    // the SAME mount-closure machinery -- omitting this parameter here
    // would special-case Sources out of a pattern every OTHER registered
    // view honors, for a "currently unreachable" reason that stops being
    // true the instant a future view hosts Sources. One-line-justified per
    // the ruling; not cheap enough to prove with a test today (there is no
    // fourth host to mount it FROM).
    [Parameter] public bool? SplitMode { get; set; }

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        if (SplitMode is null)
        {
            // The standalone counterpart to Reader/World's own EnterSingle
            // reconciliation -- asserted once, at mount (Sources has no
            // per-navigation route params to react to repeatedly the way
            // World's from/to/ref query does).
            ViewArrangementAtom.Dispatch(new EnterSingle(ViewNames.Sources));
        }

        try
        {
            _doc = await Atlas.Sources();
            // S-m1 (batch-s-review.md trivia): group once, here, rather than
            // re-scanning the full source list with a fresh LINQ `Where` on
            // every render for every category (the markup's own @foreach
            // over categories was calling `SourcesFor` once per category,
            // per render). Immaterial at today's 18-source/5-category size
            // (as the review itself noted), but memoizing costs nothing and
            // removes the re-scan entirely.
            _byCategory = _doc.Sources
                .GroupBy(s => s.Category)
                .ToDictionary(g => g.Key, g => (IReadOnlyList<SourceEntryDto>)g.ToList());
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            _error = "Couldn't load the sources list -- try refreshing the page.";
        }
    }

    private static readonly IReadOnlyList<SourceEntryDto> EmptySources = Array.Empty<SourceEntryDto>();

    private Dictionary<string, IReadOnlyList<SourceEntryDto>> _byCategory = new();

    private IReadOnlyList<SourceEntryDto> SourcesFor(string categoryId) =>
        _byCategory.TryGetValue(categoryId, out var sources) ? sources : EmptySources;
}
